Business modules live here, one directory per bounded context (SDD 5).

Each module owns its tables, exposes a published interface through index.ts and
communicates outward only through that interface or through domain events. The
ESLint dependency rule in @leen-mart/config/eslint/node enforces both of those
constraints at build time.

Expected layout, per SDD 25.2:

  modules/<name>/
    domain/          entities, value objects, events, state machines, errors
    application/     use cases, ports, DTOs
    infrastructure/  Prisma repositories, gateways, mappers
    interface/       routers, controllers, Zod schemas, job handlers
    <name>.module.ts DI wiring
    index.ts         published interface — the only legal cross-module import

No business module is implemented in this scaffold by design.
